{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB hub felt useful because my USB adapter and expansion-card purchases suggest a recurring need to connect accessories; accessible ports and individual switches give it a clear purpose for me.",
    "Ethernet cables connect naturally to my recent USB-to-Ethernet adapter purchase, so the connection was relevant even though this particular pack did not fit an established need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Internal drives, memory cards, and a CPU cooler address storage or maintenance needs that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "The Echo Dot and Fire TV Stick felt unrelated to my practical connection needs, while the HDMI cable assumed a display connection I have not shown I use.",
    "Six one-foot Ethernet cables are only useful with a matching setup; interest in wired networking alone would not make me choose that pack."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning computer accessories seemed to be treated as interest in almost any computer upgrade.",
    "My interest in connecting devices seemed to extend too broadly to smart speakers and streaming devices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases point toward specific connection tasks, where connector type, compatibility, cable length, and port access determine usefulness.",
    "I interact rarely and need a clear practical use before choosing something; a related product is not enough on its own.",
    "My recent Ethernet adapter gives networking accessories a clearer connection to my needs than storage or cooling products, but it does not establish the cable lengths or quantities I need."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my need to connect accessories but stretched that interest into unrelated electronics and upgrades."
}"}
